# POS plan authority and provenance

This directory contains POS implementation coordination, research, and
historical plan provenance. Its `active` path is an organizational location;
it does not make every plan current, accepted, executable, complete, or
canonical product truth.

## Start here

1. Read the current Product Canon in
   [`glc-works/hfeit-product`](https://github.com/glc-works/hfeit-product) at
   merged revision `a3a702f5a0c878a784c05c24afdccc365db0f496`.
2. Check the plan's current GitHub issue, delivery status, sole-writer claim,
   exact file fence, dependencies, and latest implementation evidence.
3. Follow `DEVELOPMENT.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, and the repository coordination
   rules before treating a plan as executable.

Product PR
[`glc-works/hfeit-product#60`](https://github.com/glc-works/hfeit-product/pull/60)
at exact head `fd25b91a52dc544e4e027bb579d988eeb515ca82`
proposes the broader Canon convergence and legacy-plan disposition record. It
is review evidence only while open and does not become current authority until
merged.

## Authority boundary

- Product Canon owns shared product meaning, capability boundaries, and
  accepted product decisions.
- Hfe CORE owns governed business and financial truth. A POS plan cannot
  authorize local price, tax, settlement, semantic-account, Posting, or other
  shadow financial truth.
- Identity owns first-party sign-in and federation for the Hfeit Console
  family. Identity is not customer-configurable IAM. Historical references to
  “ToGrow Account” as product authority are provenance; `account-togrow`,
  `account.togrow.id`, issuer, keys, database, cookie, and origin remain
  implementation/runtime provenance unless a separately accepted migration
  says otherwise.
- Product issue
  [`glc-works/hfeit-product#68`](https://github.com/glc-works/hfeit-product/issues/68)
  owns Experience shipping selection. Repository name, contributor origin, or
  old “canonical” wording does not preselect `hfe-pos`.
- Deployment, provider, DNS, IAM, runtime, release, and workflow mutation each
  require their own current authority and evidence. A plan or successful local
  test grants none of them.

## How to use these records

Use a plan as current execution coordination only when all of the following are
true:

- its owning issue and required Product decision are current;
- the repository dispatcher permits the work and no other claim overlaps;
- the exact base revision, dependency state, and file fence have been
  refreshed;
- the plan's assertions still match current code and contracts.

Otherwise preserve the plan as research or implementation provenance. Do not
rewrite historical bodies to make them look current. Add a current pointer or
classification at the entry boundary or through the owning issue.

Routes, UI, schemas, generated clients, tests, or green CI are evidence only.
They do not by themselves prove implementation, consumer adoption, production
deployment, or authority.
